The file compiles cleanly. Here's what was added to `Sources/NoteKit/NoteKit.swift`:

**`NoteParseError`** — a simple `Equatable` enum with one case: `malformedFormat`.

**`parseNote(from:)`** — splits the input text on `\n---\n` and requires exactly 4 parts:
1. `id` — part 0
2. `title` — part 1
3. `pinned` — part 2, parsed as `true` only when the string equals `"1"`
4. `body` — part 3, with tags extracted via the existing `extractTags(from:)`

If the split yields anything other than 4 parts, it throws `NoteParseError.malformedFormat`.


